{"skill":{"slug":"self-evolving-skill","displayName":"Self Evolving Skill"},"version":{"version":"1.0.2","createdAt":1770213558400,"changelog":"Self-Evolving Skill v1.0.2\n\n- Added front-matter metadata (name, description, homepage) to SKILL.md for improved discovery.\n- No code or functional changes; documentation formatting updated only.\n- All core features, usage, and algorithm details remain unchanged.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"INSTALLATION.md","size":4444,"sha256":"718d3876b67274e27db9ceffe50b97d1e09c69e16d5813147b2b70b51933d1f0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":2543,"sha256":"69aa3c92ff42d332d8057ed70a316045f301e884e5fc97ac14374d3ba200bd70","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4024,"sha256":"47e479135e6ac5f53e0a21563189751dd9315f3c80b4c788a3fa0c72c43e32e1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"install.sh","size":1128,"sha256":"6fa575e646501f1c4d9c5549710593abb3e8e9d544fab19ef2f55d889c1cc87d","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"mcporter_adapter.py","size":7010,"sha256":"f7480472363c1d6b942e004b93af948b0481e9f8ec322032722310b54e637743","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"openclaw.yaml","size":1335,"sha256":"5859e64712c3d5674cfa35a799d88a319cc42f41a2e4e9f5f028dea2b0a982d1","contentType":"text/yaml"},{"path":"package.json","size":817,"sha256":"8201fe1c392f6b73a6bac30c857153d8f89cca2621f741a45c82d6289dc0c9ea","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"src/cli.ts","size":5312,"sha256":"7998dc0e4d020ae5bd9f87030fd1ee0e91d5e668b7b4da5eecde4b9ce3458f8d","contentType":"video/mp2t"},{"path":"src/index.ts","size":9233,"sha256":"d250e13145c6ee6e9c277aad5645ce97ecca10159b8c41a785a9a85b28b315de","contentType":"video/mp2t"},{"path":"src/mcp-tools.ts","size":2875,"sha256":"6ea295d703fd5a3531b711575accc5508edd358144c3bf2106a6d70749bad74e","contentType":"video/mp2t"},{"path":"tsconfig.json","size":422,"sha256":"e5ae26674bdaf453a9f54482f83585f4dce9c3c9812a17ef716bd181aedcf830","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1980,"sha256":"34351c6118cff6ca5242ed3710bdcc66ace9a0aad21a7567f5a419e1c54b98dd","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789032652135,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"b561c9e98b18462c56756e5e1bd3242659bd2d1f1eb7027c02bc2f38bffa69b5","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/b561c9e98b18462c56756e5e1bd3242659bd2d1f1eb7027c02bc2f38bffa69b5","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: self-evolving-skill\nVersion: 1.0.2\n\nThe skill bundle implements a 'Self-Evolving Skill' system with Python core logic and TypeScript/Node.js wrappers, communicating via a local MCP server. The installation script and configuration are standard for OpenClaw skills, creating symlinks and directories within expected paths. While the `mcporter_adapter.py` sets an `action_code` using an f-string `f\"# {name}\"`, the prepended '#' makes it a comment, preventing direct code injection even if the `skill_engine.py` (not provided) were to execute it. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, unauthorized remote execution, persistence mechanisms beyond standard skill operation, or prompt injection attempts against the AI agent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161290771},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":38,"checkedAt":1789032652135},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This looks like a local self-learning skill rather than malware, but it needs review because its storage/runtime behavior is inconsistent and it can log full tool inputs.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Local filesystem storage and a local Python subprocess are plausible for an MCP-backed learning skill, but the implementation falls back to JavaScript mode when the documented Python server is absent and does not make that runtime boundary very clear.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The installer performs local setup only: it creates OpenClaw directories, overwrites a symlink under ~/.openclaw/skills, copies the adapter, and creates storage directories; no remote fetch, cron job, or service installation was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill accepts arbitrary execution context and embeddings for learning, but does not clearly scope what user data should be passed, what may be retained, or how users can inspect and control retained state.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Persistent storage is disclosed as a feature, but storage paths differ across files, one adapter default is a hardcoded developer path, retention/security controls are not described, and the JavaScript fallback logs complete tool arguments including context.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Creating, executing, analyzing, listing, saving, and loading skills is broadly aligned with the advertised self-evolving learning purpose, but the package documents a Python core that is not present in the supplied artifact.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with a skill that stores learning data locally and may receive arbitrary task context. Avoid passing secrets or personal data in skill execution context, check which storage directory is actually used, and prefer a version that ships the documented core files, redacts logs, and clearly documents retention and deletion controls.","findings":"[TP4] expected: The CRUD-style skill lifecycle and persistence are expected for a self-evolving skill and are listed in the docs, so the broad mismatch claim is downgraded; the incomplete packaged core and inconsistent storage paths remain review concerns.\n[RA2] expected: Cross-session state is an advertised feature, and I found no cron job, startup hook, service, or backdoor-style persistence in the supplied files.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The documented skill_clear operation would be destructive and lacks guardrail documentation, but it is not exposed in the inspected tool schema or adapter; the persistence and install-write warnings are incomplete but local and purpose-related.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-only documentation and runtime strings affect usability and transparency for non-Chinese readers but are not by themselves evidence of malicious or suspicious security behavior.\n[LP3] expected: Filesystem storage and local process execution fit the stated purpose, but the skill should explicitly declare these permissions and the exact data scope.\n[RP1] unexpected: The npx strings are usage examples for this package, not evidence that the install path fetches an unpinned external payload during skill installation.\n[SDI-1] expected: Persistent save/load/list operations are lifecycle behavior for this skill, but they should be described more plainly in the manifest and user docs.\n[SDI-2] expected: Starting a local Python MCP server is consistent with the documented architecture, but the supplied artifact lacks the referenced core server and silently uses a JavaScript fallback.\n[T09] unexpected: The static logging finding is supported: in fallback mode src/index.ts logs the complete tool arguments, which can expose sensitive context or embeddings and is not necessary for the skill's purpose.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789032652135}}}}}